# tooling caches
/.serena
# Ignore .claude/ contents but keep the design docs in .claude/docs/ tracked.
# All three lines are load-bearing, in this order:
#   1. un-ignore the directory itself — the user's global excludesFile
#      (~/.gitignore_global) ignores `.claude/`, and git will not descend into an
#      excluded directory, so no negation below it can take effect until this
#      repo-level rule (higher precedence) re-admits it;
#   2. ignore the *contents* rather than the directory, because git cannot
#      re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded;
#   3. re-include the design docs.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/docs/
.env*
